cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or data, please cite the manuscript and this repository."
title: "pm25-lima-wavelet: Reproducible wavelet multiscale analysis of the Lima PM2.5 monitoring network"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Aquino-Mosquera"
    given-names: "Henry S."
  - family-names: "Villanueva-Ramirez"
    given-names: "Jaime E."
  - family-names: "Huaman-Cardenas"
    given-names: "Daniel A."
  - family-names: "Quispe-Mendoza"
    given-names: "Gualberto R."
version: "1.0.0"
repository-code: "https://github.com/jelincovil/pm25-lima-wavelet"
date-released: "2026-10-17"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - air quality
  - PM2.5
  - wavelet transform
  - functional ANOVA
  - environmental monitoring
  - Lima
  - Peru
  - reproducibility
abstract: >-
  Analysis code, processed data, audit trail, figures and LaTeX source for a
  wavelet multiscale study of hourly PM2.5 at five REMCA stations in Lima,
  Peru. The repository reproduces the conservative preprocessing protocol,
  the Symmlet-7 discrete wavelet transform, the assumption-checked scale-wise
  tests and the manuscript tables and figures.
notes: >-
  Affiliations are listed in the manuscript. A Zenodo DOI will be added when
  the release is archived.
